This fixture is FICTIONAL TEST INPUT. Intended path LICENSE -> cfg mode. PERIOD-FORM
of a FOREIGN copyright line (sentence-final period after a non-principal name). The
c2 (Arc 69 / stoa--y12) trailing-terminal-punctuation strip yields "Fenwick Galsworthy"
-> is_principal mismatch -> BLOCK. This is the CONTROL half of the c2 fixture pair:
it proves the trailing-strip does NOT turn a foreign-name catch into a miss (the strip
removes only a terminal period, it does not weaken the foreign-name detection).
